First Author: White
Title: Predicting expiration among potential donation after circulatory death donors at 30- and 120-min post extubation
Source number: 73

Very short summary: This retrospective multicenter US study included 4,464 potential donation-after-circulatory-death donors from three organ procurement organizations between 2014 and 2025. XGBoost models predicted circulatory death within 30 and 120 minutes after extubation; the best held-out test performance was achieved by the 61-variable model for 120-minute expiration, with ROC-AUC 0.89 and PR-AUC 0.97.

